    "q-57092": {
      "dom_id": "step-q57092",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$\\frac{3}{5}÷2=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $2$ is $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\,÷\\,2=\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 2}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
