    "q-211082": {
      "dom_id": "step-q211082",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its lowest terms, $\\frac{7}{8}÷10=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $10$ is $\\frac{1}{10}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}\\,÷\\,10=\\frac{7}{8}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{10}=\\frac{7\\times 1}{8\\times 10}=\\frac{7}{80}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
