    "q-211088": {
      "dom_id": "step-q211088",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its lowest terms, $\\frac{7}{5}÷6=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $6$ is $\\frac{1}{6}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{5}\\,÷\\,6=\\frac{7}{5}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{7\\times 1}{5\\times 6}=\\frac{7}{30}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
