    "q-57242": {
      "dom_id": "step-q57242",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$\\frac{8}{11}÷4=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $4$ is $\\frac{1}{4}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{11}\\,÷\\,4=\\frac{8}{11}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{11}\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{8\\times 1}{11\\times 4}=\\frac{8}{44}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{44}=\\frac{8÷4}{44÷4}=\\frac{2}{11}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
