    "q-100152": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100152",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$\\frac{9}{4}÷6=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $6$ is $\\frac{1}{6}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}\\,÷\\,6=\\frac{9}{4}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{9\\times 1}{4\\times 6}=\\frac{9}{24}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{9÷3}{24÷3}=\\frac{3}{8}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
