    "q-211152": {
      "dom_id": "step-q211152",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its lowest terms, $\\frac{4}{5}÷8=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $8$ is $\\frac{1}{8}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\,÷\\,8=\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{4\\times 1}{5\\times 8}=\\frac{4}{40}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{40}=\\frac{4÷4}{40÷4}=\\frac{1}{10}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
